      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Autonomous vehicle (AV) developers need reasoning models that can operate within the compute and latency constraints of an onboard system.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/running-av-reasoning-models-within-onboard-compute-and-latency-limits/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T16:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T18:15:17.063Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "NVIDIA Alpamayo 2 Edge addresses this need with an adaptive reasoning vision-language-action (VLA) model designed for real-time operation on NVIDIA DRIVE AGX Thor .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/running-av-reasoning-models-within-onboard-compute-and-latency-limits/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T16:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T18:15:17.063Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Built on the 2B Nemotron-based reasoning backbone of NVIDIA Cosmos 3 Edge and paired with a diffusion action expert, it leverages surround-camera observations, temporal context, and navigation inputs to generate Chain-of-Causation (CoC) reasoning and future driving trajectories.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/running-av-reasoning-models-within-onboard-compute-and-latency-limits/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T16:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T18:15:17.063Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Making a reasoning model compact enough for onboard deployment introduces a key challenge: preserving the quality of its reasoning and driving behavior as model size is reduced.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/running-av-reasoning-models-within-onboard-compute-and-latency-limits/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T16:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T18:15:17.063Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "A 2B-parameter Nemotron-based reasoning backbone, sized for onboard inference",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/running-av-reasoning-models-within-onboard-compute-and-latency-limits/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T16:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T18:15:17.063Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "“Within days of getting early access to Alpamayo 2 Edge, we had it running closed-loop in NuRec reconstructions of our own London street recordings.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/running-av-reasoning-models-within-onboard-compute-and-latency-limits/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T16:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T18:15:17.063Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Side-by-side comparison of Alpamayo 2 Edge running in PyTorch and with Embedl optimization, showing differences in planning speed, latency, and reasoning output",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/running-av-reasoning-models-within-onboard-compute-and-latency-limits/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T16:00:00.000Z",
